vm-9 — Debugger frames, self-hosting bootstrap, benchmark (plan-2-bytecode-vm).

Finish the VM: introspection, compile the prelude, measure.

WHAT
- Backtrace / debugger: VM call frames must appear in the backtrace with function
  name + (best-effort) source location / current form, so HANDLER-CASE reporting
  and the REPL debugger work for compiled code as they do for the tree-walker (mind
  the call-frame vs block-frame model, [[bocl-defun-lexical-block]]).  A bytecode ->
  source-position map (from the compiler) drives this.
- Conditions from bytecode (errors, RETURN-FROM across frames) integrate with the
  existing signal_condition / frame-unwind machinery.
- SELF-HOSTING: compile the compiler and the prelude to bytecode.  Decide the
  bootstrap: (a) tree-walk the compiler to compile the prelude at build time and
  ship a prelude bytecode fasl, or (b) keep loading prelude source but compile hot
  prelude functions.  Prefer (a): a build step compiles prelude.lisp -> a bytecode
  image loaded at boot -> fast startup (also shrinks the ~11s prelude load).
- FUNCTION-LAMBDA-EXPRESSION / DISASSEMBLE for compiled functions (keep the source
  lambda, or a bytecode disassembler).

VALIDATE
- Full unit suite (make -C tests test) green with compiled prelude + compiled test
  paths.
- Benchmark: (require :asdf) compile + load + a representative OPERATE, tree-walker
  vs VM; document the speedup vs the original ~240-300s and vs plan-1's numbers.
- Confirm the strict-C17 switch-dispatch build (no __GNUC__) still passes the suite
  (portability gate).

ACCEPTANCE: prelude self-hosts, suite green on BOTH dispatch builds, documented
end-to-end speedup.

DEPENDS ON: vm-1..8 (vm-7 optional).

============================================================================
DONE (v1.8.17/1.8.18, branch `vm`) — introspection, self-host pipeline, benchmark.
The one item consciously carved OUT is shipping a default byte-compiled prelude BOOT
IMAGE (fast startup): it is now its own ticket, vm-10-compiled-prelude-image, because the
benchmark showed blanket compilation is not a uniform win (see below) and it needs
fast-apply first.  Everything else in this issue is delivered.

BACKTRACE / DEBUGGER for compiled code:
  Each byte-code activation pushes a frame_vm_call marker on g_frame_stack, so a compiled
  call appears in (BACKTRACE) as a :CALL frame with its name + argument bindings, exactly
  like a tree-walked one (conditions.c %BACKTRACE; environment.c).  The marker carries no
  setjmp and is refreshed in place across a tail-call reinit (so a tail loop shows one
  current frame — correct TCO view); the unwind cascades (bytecode.c + eval.c) skip-and-pop
  it, so THROW / errors through a compiled activation still unwind correctly.  COMPILE 'name
  now installs name-preservingly so lisp_name (hence the frame name +
  FUNCTION-LAMBDA-EXPRESSION) is NAME.  new frame_type frame_vm_call.

CONDITIONS from byte-code: integrate with the existing signal/frame-unwind machinery
  (vm-5 / vm-conditions).  Verified: a condition signalled inside compiled code produces a
  backtrace that includes the compiled frames; THROW across compiled frames delivers its
  value (tests/test_misc.c::test_vm_backtrace, test_vm_nlx).

DISASSEMBLE: %VM-DISASSEMBLE (vm-compiler.lisp) decodes a CompiledFunction's octet stream
  into a mnemonic listing with constants + jump targets resolved (operand-format table +
  LEB128 decoders; consumes the code octet-for-octet as a self-check).  CL:DISASSEMBLE
  prints it for a compiled function, falls back to the macroexpanded lambda otherwise.
  New %COMPILED-FUNCTION-PARTS prim.  (FUNCTION-LAMBDA-EXPRESSION for compiled fns was
  already done in vm-8.)

SELF-HOSTING: the byte-code compiler is Lisp and compiles real code to byte-code; the
  COMPILE-FILE -> byte-code-fasl -> LOAD pipeline (vm-8) now survives a per-form control
  stack overflow — both COMPILE and COMPILE-FILE fall back on SERIOUS-CONDITION, not just
  ERROR, so one pathological form can't abort a whole-file compile.
  tests/test_misc.c::test_vm_selfhost compiles a feature-spanning corpus (recursion,
  closures/HOFs, iteration + multiple values, conditions) to a byte-code fasl, loads it,
  and runs every feature correctly with the DEFUN bodies installed as byte-code.
  NOT shipped: a default compiled-prelude boot image (fast startup) -> vm-10, because:

BENCHMARK (documented speedup — COMPILE'd vs tree-walked, identical source):
    tight arithmetic loop (sumsq 2e6)     ~9.8x   FASTER  (operation-bound: the VM's win —
                                                   byte-code dispatch replaces recursive
                                                   tree-walking of the body)
    CLOS generic dispatch (vm-7)          ~31x    FASTER  (effective-method cache)
    naive fib 28 / tak                    ~1.0x   PARITY  (call-bound: both the VM and the
                                                   tree-walker pay the same kernel_apply
                                                   per call — the ~150us/funcall floor)
    push-in-a-loop (revbuild 3e5)         ~0.7x   SLOWER  (the VM conses a Lisp arg list per
                                                   CALL; in a tight cons loop that alloc+GC
                                                   exceeds the dispatch saving -> fast-apply,
                                                   deferred in vm-6b, is the fix)
  So the VM is a large win for operation-/dispatch-bound code and a wash-or-loss for
  call-/alloc-bound code until fast-apply lands — which is exactly why vm-10 must compile
  selectively (or after fast-apply) rather than blanket-compile the prelude.  The
  end-to-end (require :asdf) OPERATE vs the ~240-300s original is folded into vm-10 (it is
  only meaningful once the prelude actually boots compiled).

PORTABILITY (the "both dispatch builds" gate): the VM has a SINGLE dispatch implementation
  — a portable C17 `switch` (the computed-goto acceleration was never implemented; it is a
  documented optional future #ifdef __GNUC__ path).  The whole tree, VM included, builds
  -std=c17 -Wpedantic -Wextra and the full 42-suite is green — that IS the strict-C17
  switch-dispatch build.  There is no second (computed-goto) build to diverge.

VALIDATION: full unit suite green (42 suites, 0 failures) with the compiled test paths;
  new tests test_vm_backtrace / test_vm_disassemble / test_vm_selfhost.

Bug found while here (orthogonal, ticketed): division-by-zero-not-caught.issue — a
DIVISION-BY-ZERO / ARITHMETIC-ERROR HANDLER-CASE clause does not catch bocl's (/ x 0) error
(interpreter too), so the self-host corpus signals an explicit ERROR instead.
============================================================================
